# Linting Workflow

## Frontend (`frontend/`)

After any substantive edit to a `.js`, `.jsx`, `.ts`, or `.tsx` file:

1. Run `npm run lint:fix` in `frontend/` — runs `oxlint --fix --fix-suggestions --fix-dangerously`
2. Use `ReadLints` on edited files to catch anything oxlint can't auto-fix
3. Fix remaining errors manually
4. Never leave a task marked complete with outstanding lint errors

## Backend (`backend/`)

After any substantive edit to a `.py` file:

1. Run `npm run lint:fix` in `backend/` — runs `ruff check --fix .`
2. Run `npm run format` in `backend/` — runs `ruff format .`
3. Use `ReadLints` on edited files to catch anything ruff can't auto-fix
4. Fix remaining errors manually
5. Never leave a task marked complete with outstanding lint errors

# No Conditional Spread

Never use `...(condition && { key: value })` to build objects conditionally. It is hard to read and obscures intent.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const payload = {
  ...(data.name !== undefined && { name: data.name }),
  ...(data.status !== undefined && { status: data.status }),
};

// ✅ GOOD
const payload: Record<string, unknown> = {};
if (data.name !== undefined) payload.name = data.name;
if (data.status !== undefined) payload.status = data.status;
```
